<title>GERMANY: Vereinsbank details shareholder structure.</title>
<headline>Vereinsbank details shareholder structure.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayerische Vereinsbank</p>
<p>gave the following outline of its shareholder structure as at</p>
<p>end-1996</p>
<p>    Shareholder		Share of capital    Share of capital</p>
<p>							   with voting rights</p>
<p>Bayerische Landesstiftung and</p>
<p>    Bayerische Forschungsstiftung    10.6 pct     5.1 pct</p>
<p>    Viag AG				  10.2 pct     10.8 pct</p>
<p>    Muenchener Rueckversicherungs AG  5.1 pct     5.4 pct</p>
<p>    Deutsche Bank AG			4.9 pct     5.2 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Bayerische Vereinsbank AG. The figures were released in the bank's annual report. Vereinsbank said the number of its shareholders had dropped some 2.4 percent in the past two years to 122,524. The proportion of small shareholders had fallen to 27 percent while institutional shareholders's share had risen to 58.4 percent. Large shareholders control 69 percent of the bank's capital. The share of foreign shareholders rose slightly to over 18 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
